From 22ea496b497caaf3a05d6647d18c024428e475e3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: morgonf <morgonf@altlinux.org>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 07:12:06 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] software_isp: Gradient corrected demosaic for packed Bayer on
 the GPU

The GPU debayer of packed raw formats interpolated bilinearly over 3x3
pixels and blurred fine detail: text on boxes two metres away was soft on
all three cameras of the OnePlus 6T.

Use the Malvar-He-Cutler demosaic (bilinear corrected by the gradient
of the colour known at the centre, 5x5) and mix it with the bilinear
values by demosaicSharpness from the tuning file (Adjust, 0 to 1, 0 is
the former behaviour). Full strength nearly triples the mean Laplacian
of a viewfinder frame but shows more grain at high gain; 0.5 for the
IMX519, IMX371 and IMX376 almost doubles it (9.9 to 17.8). Quad Bayer
frames of the IMX371 show no new artefacts.
